 border-gold/5 hover:border-gold/20\">Tantra</button><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-ui tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow bg-surface/30 text-text-muted hover:text-gold-dim border border-gold/5 hover:border-gold/20\">Meditation</button><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-ui tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow bg-surface/30 text-text-muted hover:text-gold-dim border border-gold/5 hover:border-gold/20\">Dhāraṇā</button></div></div><div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-center gap-4\"><div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-mono tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow bg-gold text-deep-black\">All Levels</button><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-mono tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow text-text-muted hover:text-gold-dim border border-gold/5 hover:border-gold/20\">Open</button><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-mono tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow text-text-muted hover:text-gold-dim border border-gold/5 hover:border-gold/20\">Moderate</button><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-mono tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow text-text-muted hover:text-gold-dim border border-gold/5 hover:border-gold/20\">High</button><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-mono tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow text-text-muted hover:text-gold-dim border border-gold/5 hover:border-gold/20\">Sealed</button></div><span class=\"hidden md:block text-text-muted/30\">·</span><div class=\"flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-mono tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow bg-gold text-deep-black\">All Tiers</button><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-mono tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow text-text-muted hover:text-gold-dim border border-gold/5 hover:border-gold/20\">Antechamber</button><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-mono tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow text-text-muted hover:text-gold-dim border border-gold/5 hover:border-gold/20\">Initiate</button><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-mono tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow text-text-muted hover:text-gold-dim border border-gold/5 hover:border-gold/20\">Practitioner</button><button class=\"px-3.5 py-2 text-[0.8125rem] font-mono tracking-[0.1em] uppercase rounded-sm transition-all duration-400 neon-chip-glow text-text-muted hover:text-gold-dim border border-gold/5 hover:border-gold/20\">The Vault</button></div></div></div><p class=\"text-caption mb-12\">Showing <!-- -->48<!-- --> of <!-- -->48</p><div class=\"grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6\" style=\"opacity:0\"><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/pranava-japa\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Pranava Japa</h3></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">प्रणव जप — Oṃkāra Repetition</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The contemplative repetition of Oṃ, the primal sound (pranava) held in the Upaniṣads to be the sonic signature of the Absolute. Oṃ is not merely a word — it is held to be the acoustic ground from which all manifestation arises and into which it dissolves. The Māṇḍūkya Upaniṣad devotes its entire twelve verses to unpacking its four quarters: the waking state (A), the dream state (U), the deep-sleep state (M), and the fourth (turīya) — the silence beyond. Patañjali&#x27;s Yoga Sūtras (I.27–28) designate Oṃ as the designator of Īśvara and hold that its repetition dissolves obstacles. This is arguably the single most widely practiced contemplative technique in the Hindu tradition, crossing all sectarian boundaries.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-green-400/80 border-green-400/15 bg-green-400/5\">OPEN</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Mantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Vedānta / Upaniṣadic</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Foundation</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/gayatri-mantra\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Gāyatrī Mantra</h3></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">गायत्री मन्त्र — Savitṛ Invocation</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">A verse from the Ṛgveda (III.62.10) invoking the radiant principle (Savitṛ) to illuminate the intellect — among the most widely transmitted invocations in the tradition. The Gāyatrī meter itself is one of the principal Vedic meters, and this particular verse has become the most recited mantra in all of Hinduism, performed daily by millions at dawn and dusk. The verse addresses Savitṛ — the impeller, the stimulating principle of the sun — requesting that the divine radiance inspire our understanding. Its ubiquity across castes, languages, and sects is unparalleled in the Hindu ritual corpus.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-green-400/80 border-green-400/15 bg-green-400/5\">OPEN</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Mantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Vedic (Ṛgveda)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Foundation</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/nadi-shuddhi\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Nāḍī Śuddhi</h3></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">नाडी शुद्धि — Channel Purification Breath</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Alternate-nostril breathing (anuloma-viloma) used to balance the lunar (iḍā) and solar (piṅgalā) vital currents before deeper practice. This is the foundational breath technique of the Haṭha Yoga system, prescribed in the Haṭha Yoga Pradīpikā (II.7–14) as the first of the eight kumbhakas. The practice is based on the model that the breath flows predominantly through one nostril at a time, alternating roughly every ninety minutes. Nāḍī Śuddhi actively equalizes this flow, producing a state the texts describe as &#x27;sushumna awakening&#x27; — a balanced, integrated awareness suitable for meditation. Modern research on the nasal cycle and its relationship to hemispheric dominance provides an interesting parallel.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-green-400/80 border-green-400/15 bg-green-400/5\">OPEN</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Prāṇāyāma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Haṭha / Rāja Yoga</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Foundation</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/soham-dhyana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">So&#x27;haṃ Dhyāna</h3></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">सोऽहं — &#x27;I Am That&#x27; Non-dual Contemplation</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Contemplative abidance in the recognition &#x27;so&#x27;haṃ&#x27; — &#x27;I am That&#x27; — the non-dual identity of the individual self (jīva) and the absolute (brahman). The Bṛhadāraṇyaka Upaniṣad (I.4.10) contains the foundational statement: &#x27;aham brahmāsmi&#x27; — &#x27;I am brahman.&#x27; The so&#x27;haṃ formulation reframes this as the natural, ever-present sound of the breath itself: &#x27;so&#x27; on the inhalation (He/That), &#x27;haṃ&#x27; on the exhalation (I am). The Nāth tradition developed this into ajapa-japa — the unrecited recitation — holding that this mantra repeats itself 21,600 times daily without effort. The practice is deceptively simple: its depth lies not in technique but in the sustained willingness to rest in the recognition it points to.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-green-400/80 border-green-400/15 bg-green-400/5\">OPEN</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Meditation</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Vedānta / Nāth</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Foundation</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/manasika-japa\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Mānasika Japa</h3></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">मानसिक जप — Mental Repetition</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The wholly internal repetition of a mantra, without movement of lips or breath — regarded as the most subtle and powerful mode of japa. The Haṭha Yoga Pradīpikā describes four stages of japa — vācaka (audible), upāṃśu (whispered), mānasika (mental), and ajapa (spontaneous) — each progressively more internal. Mānasika japa is the third stage, where the practitioner maintains the mantra entirely within the field of awareness. The Manu Smṛti (II.85) rates mental japa as ten times more potent than audible repetition. This is the bridge between technique (japa) and meditation (dhyāna) — the point where repetitive practice becomes contemplative absorption.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-green-400/80 border-green-400/15 bg-green-400/5\">OPEN</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Mantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Universal</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Foundation</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/sandhya-vandanam\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Sandhyā Vandanam</h3></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">सन्ध्यावन्दनम् — The Twilight Rites</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The thrice-daily Vedic discipline performed at the junctures (sandhyā) of dawn, noon, and dusk — arguably the oldest continuously practiced contemplative ritual on earth. The rite integrates ācamana (water purification), prāṇāyāma, Gāyatrī japa (108 repetitions), and specific mudrās and mantras into a choreographed whole. The Taittirīya Āraṇyaka and the Gṛhya Sūtras provide the earliest textual prescriptions. The ritual&#x27;s persistence — still performed daily by hundreds of thousands of Brahmin householders — makes it a living artifact of Bronze Age religion. It is presented here as a documented heritage practice with deep contemplative structure, not as a prescription for untrained practitioners.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-green-400/80 border-green-400/15 bg-green-400/5\">OPEN</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Ritual</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Vedic (Smārta)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Foundation</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/trataka\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Trāṭaka</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">त्राटक — Steady Gazing</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Fixed-gaze concentration, classically upon a candle flame, listed among the six purification acts (ṣaṭkarma) and as a gateway to inner vision.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Dhāraṇā</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Haṭha / Rāja Yoga</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/ajapa-japa\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Ajapa-Japa</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">अजपाजप — The Spontaneous Breath-Mantra</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The recognition that the breath itself sounds &#x27;haṃ-saḥ&#x27; (So&#x27;haṃ) some 21,600 times a day — japa performed without effort of repetition.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Mantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Nāth / Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/mahamrityunjaya\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Maha Mṛtyuṅjaya Mantra</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">महामृत्युंजय — The Great Death-Conquering Verse</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">A Ṛgvedic verse (VII.59.12) addressed to Tryambaka (the three-eyed one), petitioning liberation from mortality &#x27;as a cucumber from its vine.&#x27;</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Mantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Vedic (Ṛgveda)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/yoga-nidra\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Yoga Nidrā</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">योग निद्रा — Conscious Sleep</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The state of &#x27;conscious sleep&#x27; — the body resting while awareness remains luminous and unbroken, rooted in tantric and Upaniṣadic sources.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Meditation</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Tantra / Haṭha</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/bija-mantra\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Bīja Mantra</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">बीज मन्त्र — Seed Sounds of the Cakras</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The seed-syllables (laṃ, vaṃ, raṃ, yaṃ, haṃ, oṃ) associated with the six contemplative centers — sonic &#x27;seeds&#x27; held to condense an entire principle into a single phoneme.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Mantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/kumbhaka\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Kumbhaka</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">कुम्भक — Breath Retention</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The deliberate, measured retention of breath (antar/sahita) described in the Yoga Sūtras as the means by which &#x27;the veil over illumination is thinned.&#x27;</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Prāṇāyāma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Haṭha / Rāja Yoga</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/chakra-dharana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Cakra Dhāraṇā</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">चक्र धारणा — Concentration on the Centers</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Structured concentration upon the six principal psycho-spiritual centers (mūlādhāra → ājñā), each visualized with its element, color, and seed-syllable.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Dhāraṇā</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/sudarshana-chakra-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Sudarśana Chakra Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">सुदर्शन चक्र — The Discus of Viṣṇu</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Sādhana of the Sudarśana Chakra — the discus of Viṣṇu, wielded as the instrument of protective dharma. Attested in the Ahirbudhnya Saṃhitā and the Sudarśana Kavaca tradition.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śrī Vaiṣṇava (Pāñcarātra)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/kamala-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Kamalā Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">कमला — The Lotus Goddess</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The tenth Mahāvidyā, the benevolent lotus-seated form — iconographically akin to Lakṣmī, bathed by two elephants, holding lotuses. Attested in Kamalā Mahāvidyā, Śākta Praamoda, Mahābhāgavata Purāṇa.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā — tenth)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/shanti-karma\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Śānti Karma (Pacification)</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">शान्तिकर्म — The Pacifying Act</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The first of the six ṣaṭ-karma — pacification. The calming of hostile forces, the settling of disturbances, the restoration of equilibrium. Attested in the Agni Purāṇa ch. 138, Prapañcasāra Tantra, Śāradā Tilaka.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta / Ṣaṭ-karma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/sri-yantra-dhyana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Śrī Cakra Contemplation</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">श्री चक्र — The Great Yantra</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Meditative absorption upon the Śrī Yantra — nine interlocking triangles converging on a single point (bindu), the supreme geometric instrument of Śrī Vidyā.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Yantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śrī Vidyā</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/bagalamukhi-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Bagalāmukhī Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">बगलामुखी — The Paralysing Goddess</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The eighth Mahāvidyā, embodying stambhana (paralysis) — the power to silence hostile speech and arrest inauspicious force. Attested in the Todala Tantra and Rudrayāmala.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/chinnamasta-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Chinnamastā Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">चिन्नमस्ता — The Self-Decapitated Goddess</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The third Mahāvidyā, iconographically depicted as self-decapitated, holding her own severed head while her two attendants drink the three streams of blood. Attested in Śāradā Tilaka ch. 7 and Prāṇatoṣiṇī commentary.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/kala-bhairava-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Kāla Bhairava Aṣṭākṣara Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">काल भैरव — The Terrifying Form of Śiva</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Sādhana of Kāla Bhairava — the fierce, time-bound form of Śiva who guards the threshold and dissolves fear. Attested in the Svacchanda Tantra and the Kāla Bhairavāṣṭakam.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śaiva (Kashmir Śaiva / Siddhānta)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/bala-tripurasundari-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Bālā Tripurasundarī (Bālā Pañcadaśākṣarī)</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">बालात्रिपुरसुन्दरी — The Girl-Form of the Goddess</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Sādhana of Bālā Tripurasundarī — the girl-form (bālā) of the Goddess, the entry-level practice of Śrī Vidyā using the 15-syllable pañcadaśākṣarī mantra. Attested in the Vāmakeśvara Tantra and Paraśurāma Kalpasūtra.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śrī Vidyā (Śākta)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/dhumavati-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Dhūmāvatī Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">धूमावती — The Smoke-Clad Widow</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The seventh Mahāvidyā, iconographically depicted as an aged, smoke-clad widow riding a crow, embodying inauspiciousness, decay, and the wisdom of all that is rejected. Attested in Dhūmāvatī Tantra and Śākta Praamoda.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/matangi-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Mātaṅgī Sādhana (Ucchiṣṭa Caṇḍālinī)</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">मातङ्गी — The Leftover Goddess</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The tenth Mahāvidyā, in her Ucchiṣṭa Caṇḍālinī form — the goddess worshipped with leftover food, embodying the transgressive wisdom of the marginal. Attested in the Gandharva Tantra and Mātaṅgī Tantra.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/tara-ugra-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Tārā (Ugra) Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">उग्रतारा — The Fierce Hindu Tārā</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The second Mahāvidyā, the Hindu Ugra Tārā form — distinct from Tibetan Green Tārā — depicted standing on a corpse in the cremation ground. Attested in the Bṛhad Nīla Tantra and the Tārā Tantra.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/tripura-bhairavi-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Tripura Bhairavī Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">त्रिपुरभैरवी — The Fierce Form of Tripurasundarī</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The sixth Mahāvidyā, the fierce form of Tripurasundarī in the Śrī Vidyā canon. Attested in Śāradā Tilaka ch. 11 and the Paraśurāma Kalpasūtra.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śrī Vidyā (Śākta)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/smasana-bhairavi-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Smāśāna Bhairavī Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">श्मशानभैरवी — The Cremation-Ground Goddess</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Sādhana of Smāśāna Bhairavī — the cremation-ground form of the Goddess in the Bhairavī strand of Śaiva-Śākta tantra. Attested in the Brahmayāmala Tantra and the Jayadrathayāmala.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śaiva-Śākta (Bhairavī strand)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/guhyakali-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Guhyakālī Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">गुह्यकाली — The Secret Kālī</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Sādhana of Guhyakālī — the &#x27;Secret Kālī&#x27; in her 64-fold form, iconographically depicted with ten arms and fifty heads. Attested in the Guhyakālī Tantra and the Mahākāla Saṃhitā Guhyakālī Khaṇḍa.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta-Kālī (Mahākāla Saṃhitā)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/dakshina-kali-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Dakṣiṇa Kālī Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">दक्षिणकाली — The Benevolent Fierce Form</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The primary Mahāvidyā form of Kālī — the first of the ten Mahāvidyās, iconographically depicted standing on Śiva, four-armed, holding a cleaver and a severed head, wearing a garland of severed heads and a skirt of severed arms. Attested in the Karpūrādi Stotra, Kālī Tantra, Todala Tantra.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā — first)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/shodashi-tripurasundari-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Ṣoḍaśī / Tripurasundarī Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">षोडशी — The Sixteen-Year-Old Goddess</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The full pañcadaśākṣarī (15-syllable) sādhana of Tripurasundarī — the beautiful sixteen-year-old form of the Goddess, the central deity of Śrī Vidyā. Attested in the Vāmakeśvara Tantra, Bhāvanā Upaniṣad, Paraśurāma Kalpasūtra.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śrī Vidyā (Śākta)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/bhuvaneshvari-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Bhuvaneśvarī Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">भुवनेश्वरी — Queen of the Universe</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The fourth Mahāvidyā, the &#x27;Queen of the Universe&#x27; form of the Goddess — three-eyed, four-armed, holding a noose and a goad, seated on a throne. Attested in Śāradā Tilaka, Bhuvaneśvarī Tantra, and the Rudrayāmala.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā — fourth)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/bhairavi-proper-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Bhairavī Sādhana (Proper)</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">भैरवी — The Teacher Goddess</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The fifth Mahāvidyā in her proper form — distinct from Tripura Bhairavī — seated on a corpse, holding a rosary and a book, embodying the teacher aspect of the Goddess. Attested in Bhairavī Tantra, Rudrayāmala, Śāradā Tilaka.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta (Daśa Mahāvidyā — fifth)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/preta-siddhi\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Preta-Saṁvāda (Spirit Dialogue)</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">प्रेतसंवाद — Dialogue with the Departed</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">A complete Aghora/Kaula field rite for invoking, questioning, and releasing a preta (restless spirit) within a protected maṇḍala. Documented in the supplied Preta-Siddhi field manual.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Tantra / Aghora / Kaula</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/vajrayogini-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Vajravārāhī / Vajrayoginī Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">वज्रवाराही — The Adamantine Sow-Headed Ḍākinī</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Sādhana of Vajravārāhī (Vajrayoginī) — the adamantine sow-headed ḍākinī of the Cakrasaṃvara cycle. Attested in the Śrī Vajravārāhīsādhana and the Cakrasaṃvara-tantra.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Buddhist Tantra (Cakrasaṃvara cycle)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/pratyangira-devi-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Pratyaṅgirā Devī Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">प्रत्यङ्गिरा — The Atharvaṇa Protective Goddess</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">Sādhana of Pratyaṅgirā Devī — the protective goddess of the Atharvaṇa tradition, invoked to neutralise hostile force. Attested in the Atharvānokta Pratyaṅgirā Vidhāna and Pratyaṅgirā Kalpa.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta (Atharvaṇa / Aghora)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/lakulisha-pashupata-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Lakulīśa Pāśupata Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">लाकुलीश पाशुपत — The Pāśupata Ascetic Path</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The Pāśupata Śaiva ascetic path attributed to Lakulīśa (2nd c. CE) — the elder Śaiva tradition that influenced later tantra. Attested in the Pāśupata Sūtras with Kauṇḍinya&#x27;s Pañcārthabhāṣya (Trivandrum Sanskrit Series 143, 1940).</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śaiva (Pāśupata)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/matsyendranath-nath-sadhana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Matsyendranāth / Nāth Sādhana</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">मत्स्येन्द्रनाथ — The Nāth Siddha Tradition</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The Nāth Siddha tradition attributed to Matsyendranāth — the yogic-astral-body lineage that influenced Haṭha Yoga and the later tantric traditions. Attested in the Kaulajñānanirṇaya, Swacchanda Tantra with Kṣemarāja&#x27;s commentary, and the Khecarīvidyā.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Nāth (Śaiva-Yogic)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/vashikarana-karma\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Vaśīkaraṇa Karma (Subjugation)</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">वशीकरणकर्म — The Subduing Act</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The second of the six ṣaṭ-karma — subjugation. Bringing someone under one&#x27;s influence. Attested in the Agni Purāṇa, Prapañcasāra Tantra, Rudrayāmala, Mantra Mahodadhi.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta / Ṣaṭ-karma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/stambhana-karma\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Stambhana Karma (Immobilization)</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">स्तम्भनकर्म — The Paralysing Act</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The third of the six ṣaṭ-karma — immobilization. Arresting motion, speech, or intent. Attested in the Agni Purāṇa, Prapañcasāra, Mahānirvāṇa Tantra (stone kalāśa), Todala Tantra (Bagalāmukhī as presiding Mahāvidyā).</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta / Ṣaṭ-karma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/vidveshana-karma\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Vidveṣaṇa Karma (Discord-Generation)</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">विद्वेषणकर्म — The Dividing Act</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The fourth of the six ṣaṭ-karma — discord-generation. Creating division between enemies. Attested in the Agni Purāṇa, Prapañcasāra, Mahānirvāṇa Tantra, Brahmayāmala.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta / Ṣaṭ-karma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/uccatana-karma\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Uccāṭana Karma (Driving Away)</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">उच्चाटनकर्म — The Expelling Act</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The fifth of the six ṣaṭ-karma — driving away. Forcing a hostile force to depart. Attested in the Agni Purāṇa, Prapañcasāra, Mahānirvāṇa Tantra, Mantra Mahodadhi.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta / Ṣaṭ-karma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/marana-karma\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Māraṇa Karma (Transformation/Death)</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">मारणकर्म — The Severing Act</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The sixth and most severe of the six ṣaṭ-karma — transformation/death. The severing of a hostile force. Attested in the Agni Purāṇa, Prapañcasāra, Mahānirvāṇa Tantra, Mantra Mahodadhi.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta / Ṣaṭ-karma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/nyasa-steps\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Nyāsa — The Art of Placing</h3></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">न्यास — Touch-Placement Rite</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The foundational tantric rite of nyāsa — the ritual &#x27;placing&#x27; of bīja-syllables on specific body parts using the fingertips, accompanied by breath and intention. Nyāsa is not a sādhana in itself but the preliminary technology that makes all other sādhana possible: it installs the deity&#x27;s presence in the practitioner&#x27;s body-vehicle before any japa, dhvāna, or dhyāna can proceed. Documented across the entire tantric corpus — from the Śāradā Tilaka to the Prapañcasāra to every modern paddhati. The rite exists in multiple forms: kara-nyāsa (hand-placement), aṅga-nyāsa (limb-placement), mātṛkā-nyāsa (alphabet-placement), and ṣaḍaṅga-nyāsa (six-limbed placement of the six limbs with oṃ, hrīṁ, śrīṁ, aiṃ, klīṁ, sauḥ).</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-green-400/80 border-green-400/15 bg-green-400/5\">OPEN</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Ritual</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Tantra (Universal Preliminary)</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Foundation</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/personalized-bija-mantra\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Personalized Bīja Mantra Guide</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">बीज मन्त्र — Personalized Seed-Sound Assignment</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">The traditional method for determining an individual&#x27;s personal bīja-mantra based on their natal Moon (janma rāśi) and nakṣatra. This is not a single sādhana but a framework — a decision-tree documented across multiple paddhatis that connects a person&#x27;s birth-star to one of the principal bīja-syllables, then prescribes the appropriate devatā, mudrā, and count. The system represents the intersection of jyotiṣa (Vedic astrology) and mantra-śāstra — two of the six Vedāṅgas working in concert. The methodology varies by lineage: some systems assign by nakṣatra alone, others cross-reference the Moon&#x27;s navāṃśa position, and still others use the name-based akṣara calculation.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Mantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Tantra / Jyotiṣa</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/five-rare-breath-techniques\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Five Rare Breath Techniques</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">पञ्च विरल प्राणायाम — Five Uncommon Prāṇāyāma</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">A collection of five uncommon breath techniques drawn from tantric and Haṭha sources that go beyond the standard eight kumbhakas of the Haṭha Yoga Pradīpikā. These include techniques that combine breath retention with bīja-repetition, specific ratios for activating individual cakras, and methods that use the breath to prepare the subtle body for tantric visualization. The techniques represent the bridge between classical prāṇāyāma (as codified in the HYP and Gheraṇḍa Saṃhitā) and the more specialized breathwork found in tantric paddhatis.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-yellow-400/80 border-yellow-400/15 bg-yellow-400/5\">MODERATE</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Prāṇāyāma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Tantra / Haṭha</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Intermediate</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/agni-marana-tantra\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Agni Māraṇa Tantra</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">अग्नि मारण तन्त्र — The Fire Severance Tantra</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">A specific tantric text documenting the fire-based māraṇa (severance) rite — one of the most restricted categories in the ṣaṭ-karma system. The Agni Māraṇa Tantra prescribes the use of agni (fire) as the primary kalāśa element for the most severe of the six acts. Documented as a standalone tantra rather than as a chapter within a larger compendium, suggesting it was intended as a specialized reference for ācāryas already grounded in the broader ṣaṭ-karma framework. This document is preserved as heritage scholarship — the rite is documented, analyzed, and contextualized within the history of Indian occult practice. It is not and will never be operationalized as a feature of KALKI.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta / Ṣaṭ-karma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/stambhana-marana-combined\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Stambhana-Māraṇa — The Freezing Death</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">स्तम्भन मारण — The Paralysing Severance</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">A combined rite that fuses stambhana (immobilization) with māraṇa (severance) — representing the most concentrated form of the ṣaṭ-karma system where two destructive acts are chained into a single operational sequence. The text documents the specific procedural requirements for combining the stone kalāśa (stambhana) with the skull-bowl kalāśa (māraṇa), including the transitional mantras and the specific timing constraints. This is among the most restricted material in the entire archive. Documented as heritage scholarship — never operationalized.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta / Ṣaṭ-karma</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/virudha-ahara-marana\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Vīrudha-Āhāra Māraṇa</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">विरूढआहार मारण — The Energetic Food-Poison Curse</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">A specific māraṇa variant that operates through the medium of food — the most intimate and insidious form of the severance act. The Vīrudha-Āhāra Māraṇa documents the method of charging food substances with destructive intention through specific mantras and rituals, then introducing them into the target&#x27;s diet. This text sits at the intersection of the Śākta ṣaṭ-karma system and the Atharvaṇa tradition of food-based magic. Documented as heritage scholarship — this is the forbidden knowledge the brand promises, preserved, not performed.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono text-copper border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\">SEALED</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta / Ṣaṭ-karma / Atharvaṇa</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Restricted</span></div></div></a></div><div style=\"opacity:0;transform:translateY(20px)\"><a class=\"glass-chip group flex flex-col\" href=\"/archive/nimbu-mantra-siddhi\"><div class=\"p-6 md:p-8 flex flex-col gap-4 flex-1\"><div class=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-4\"><div class=\"flex-1 min-w-0\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-1.5\"><h3 class=\"font-display text-xl md:text-2xl text-foreground leading-tight tracking-tight group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Nimbu Mantra Siddhi — The Lemon Rite</h3><span class=\"shrink-0 w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated flex items-center justify-center border border-gold/10\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-lock w-3 h-3 text-gold-dim\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect width=\"18\" height=\"11\" x=\"3\" y=\"11\" rx=\"2\" ry=\"2\"></rect><path d=\"M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4\"></path></svg></span></div><p class=\"text-sm text-gold-dim font-mono tracking-wider\">निम्बु मन्त्र सिद्धि — Lemon Mantra Accomplishment</p></div></div><p class=\"text-base text-text-secondary leading-relaxed line-clamp-3 editorial-spacing\">A specific tantric siddhi involving the ritual use of a lemon (nimbu) as the primary object of mantra-charging and subsequent application. The lemon rite exists in multiple variants across Indian folk-tantric practice — some benevolent (protective, purificatory), others malefic (curse-delivery). The text documents the specific mantras, the preparation of the lemon, the charging protocol, and the prescribed applications. This siddhi sits at the boundary between learned tradition and folk practice, making it particularly valuable as evidence of how tantric technology migrated from textual tradition to lived practice.</p><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3 mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-gold/5\"><span class=\"text-[0.8125rem] px-2.5 py-1 rounded-sm border tracking-[0.15em] uppercase font-mono border-copper/30 bg-copper/5\" style=\"color:var(--crimson);border-color:rgba(138, 37, 44, 0.35)\">HIGH</span><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><div class=\"w-full h-1.5 rounded-full bg-surface-elevated overflow-hidden\"><span class=\"block h-full rounded-full\" style=\"background:var(--gold);width:0%\"></span></div></div><div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\"><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-copper\">Śākta / Folk Tantra</span><div class=\"flex-1\"></div><span class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] tracking-[0.12em] uppercase text-text-muted\">Advanced</span></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"mt-32\"><div class=\"divider-gold mb-16\"></div><div class=\"flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-end md:justify-between gap-6 mb-12\"><div><p class=\"section-label mb-4\">The Pattern Taxonomy</p><h2 class=\"font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl text-foreground font-light tracking-[0.06em] engraved-heading\">Ten Mahāvidyās<!-- --> —<!-- --> Ten Karmic Loops</h2></div><a class=\"ghost-cta inline-block w-fit\" href=\"/archetypes\">Enter the Wheel</a></div><div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-5 gap-4\"><a class=\"glass-chip p-5 group text-center\" href=\"/archetypes#kali\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim mb-2 tracking-[0.2em]\">01</p><p class=\"font-display text-2xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Kālī</p><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted mt-1.5 tracking-[0.1em] line-clamp-2\">The loop of ego-attachment that must be severed</p></a><a class=\"glass-chip p-5 group text-center\" href=\"/archetypes#tara\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim mb-2 tracking-[0.2em]\">02</p><p class=\"font-display text-2xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Tārā</p><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted mt-1.5 tracking-[0.1em] line-clamp-2\">The loop of drowning / needing to be ferried across</p></a><a class=\"glass-chip p-5 group text-center\" href=\"/archetypes#chinnamasta\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim mb-2 tracking-[0.2em]\">03</p><p class=\"font-display text-2xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Chinnamastā</p><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted mt-1.5 tracking-[0.1em] line-clamp-2\">The loop of self-sacrifice / feeding others from your own life-force</p></a><a class=\"glass-chip p-5 group text-center\" href=\"/archetypes#bhuvaneshvari\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim mb-2 tracking-[0.2em]\">04</p><p class=\"font-display text-2xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Bhuvaneśvarī</p><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted mt-1.5 tracking-[0.1em] line-clamp-2\">The loop of control / cosmic-sovereignty wound</p></a><a class=\"glass-chip p-5 group text-center\" href=\"/archetypes#shodashi\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim mb-2 tracking-[0.2em]\">05</p><p class=\"font-display text-2xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Ṣoḍaśī / Tripurasundarī</p><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted mt-1.5 tracking-[0.1em] line-clamp-2\">The loop of beauty-as-avoidance</p></a><a class=\"glass-chip p-5 group text-center\" href=\"/archetypes#bhairavi\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim mb-2 tracking-[0.2em]\">06</p><p class=\"font-display text-2xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Bhairavī</p><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted mt-1.5 tracking-[0.1em] line-clamp-2\">The loop of refusing the teacher</p></a><a class=\"glass-chip p-5 group text-center\" href=\"/archetypes#dhumavati\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim mb-2 tracking-[0.2em]\">07</p><p class=\"font-display text-2xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Dhūmāvatī</p><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted mt-1.5 tracking-[0.1em] line-clamp-2\">The loop of inauspiciousness / widowhood-of-the-soul</p></a><a class=\"glass-chip p-5 group text-center\" href=\"/archetypes#bagalamukhi\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim mb-2 tracking-[0.2em]\">08</p><p class=\"font-display text-2xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Bagalāmukhī</p><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted mt-1.5 tracking-[0.1em] line-clamp-2\">The loop of being silenced / needing to freeze a hostile force</p></a><a class=\"glass-chip p-5 group text-center\" href=\"/archetypes#matangi\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim mb-2 tracking-[0.2em]\">09</p><p class=\"font-display text-2xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Mātaṅgī</p><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-text-muted mt-1.5 tracking-[0.1em] line-clamp-2\">The loop of transgressive voice / the outcaste within</p></a><a class=\"glass-chip p-5 group text-center\" href=\"/archetypes#kamala\"><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-gold-dim mb-2 tracking-[0.2em]\">10</p><p class=\"font-display text-2xl text-foreground group-hover:text-gold transition-colors duration-500 font-light\">Kamalā</p><p class=\"font-mono text-[0.75rem] text-tex